WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:04.371
While more than a million Game of Thrones
fans found no issue crying out for HBO to

00:00:04.371 --> 00:00:08.120
remake the eighth and final season with a
different group of writers, actress Sophie

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:12.219
Turner feels their protests to be incredibly
rude. And of course, if you didn't realize

00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:16.440
by now: major spoilers ahead concerning the
series finale of Game of Thrones!

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:22.160
Turner, who portrayed Sansa Stark on the series
from its premiere episode in 2011 to its series

00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:27.000
finale in 2019, addressed the recent fan petition
that's been making headlines in an interview

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:27.880
with The New York Times.

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:33.000
Created by a Change.org user known only as
"Dylan D," the appeal slams Game of Thrones

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:37.920
series creators, showrunners, and frequent
directors David Benioff and D.B. Weiss.

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:40.300
The petition accuses Benioff and Weiss of
being:

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:44.760
"[...] woefully incompetent writers when they
have no source material (i.e. the books) to

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:45.480
fall back on."

00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:46.920
"He--"

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:50.620
He, what? What does he say about me?"

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:56.140
It also demands that HBO hire a team of, quote,
"competent writers" to create "a final season

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:57.140
that makes sense."

00:00:57.260 --> 00:01:01.079
When asked for her thoughts about the uproar
from fans which reached an apex when the newly

00:01:01.079 --> 00:01:05.530
minted Mad Queen Daenerys Targaryen set King's
Landing ablaze in the series' second-to-last

00:01:05.530 --> 00:01:06.880
episode Turner responded:

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:11.520
"[...] I think [the petition] is disrespectful
to the crew, and the writers, and the filmmakers

00:01:11.530 --> 00:01:16.390
who have worked tirelessly over 10 years [...] So
many people worked so, so hard on it, and

00:01:16.390 --> 00:01:20.740
for people to just rubbish it because it's
not what they want to see is just disrespectful."

00:01:21.020 --> 00:01:25.690
As Turner notes, Game of Thrones has been
subverting expectations since the very beginning,

00:01:25.690 --> 00:01:29.329
so why should it change course during the
final season? The actress told The New York

00:01:29.329 --> 00:01:29.820
Times:

00:01:30.329 --> 00:01:33.460
"The thing about Game of Thrones that's always
been amazing is the fact that there's always

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:38.200
been crazy twists and turns, right from [season
one] with Ned's beheading. So Daenerys becoming

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:41.770
something of the Mad Queen — it shouldn't
be such a negative thing for fans. It's a

00:01:41.770 --> 00:01:44.680
shock for sure, but I think it's just because
it hasn't gone their way."

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:49.180
Turner is far from the first Game of Thrones
star to speak out about audience backlash.

00:01:49.190 --> 00:01:53.270
Kit Harington, who portrayed her onscreen
brother-slash-cousin Jon Snow, told Esquire

00:01:53.270 --> 00:01:57.970
in April that any critic who makes a "negative
judgement" on the final season can, quote,

00:01:57.970 --> 00:02:02.210
"go f--- themselves," as he feels they don't
fully understand how difficult it is to make

00:02:02.210 --> 00:02:05.700
even one episode of Game of Thrones. Harington
told the publication:

00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:10.360
"I know how much people cared about this.
I know how much pressure people put on themselves

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:14.450
and I know how many sleepless nights working
or otherwise people had on this show [...] Because

00:02:14.450 --> 00:02:18.640
they cared about not letting people down.
Now if people feel let down by it, I don't

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:19.940
give a f---. That's how I feel."

00:02:20.570 --> 00:02:24.660
The woman whose character's downfall catalyzed
the demand for a season 8 remake, Daenerys

00:02:24.670 --> 00:02:29.390
Targaryen actress Emilia Clarke, also recently
opened up about the fan petition. Speaking

00:02:29.390 --> 00:02:32.880
with The New Yorker, Clarke revealed that
the Mother of Dragons falling from grace to

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:37.240
become the Mad Queen and then facing the ultimate
betrayal when Jon Snow murders her, quote,

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:40.870
"seemed like the only way it could end" for
Dany. Clarke told The New Yorker:

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:45.220
"It absolutely breaks my heart that anyone
would think anything bad of her. But I'm sure

00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:48.360
they will, and I can't control that. I don't
know that there was any other way."

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:53.400
On the other hand, Turner's character completed
her arc in an almost universally loved way.

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:57.450
After members of the remaining Great Houses
of Westeros met with one another and agreed

00:02:57.450 --> 00:03:01.761
with Tyrion Lannister's suggestion that Bran
Stark should be crowned as the new king, Sansa

00:03:01.761 --> 00:03:05.830
declared that the North would separate itself
from the other kingdoms, stand independent,

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:10.680
and never vote on who will become the protector
of the Realm. Everyone supported Sansa, and

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:14.000
when she returned home to Winterfell, she
was crowned the Queen in the North.

00:03:14.140 --> 00:03:15.500
Turner said of Sansa's ending:

00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:20.020
"I loved it. It's the only place that she
really, truly feels safe. The place that she's

00:03:20.030 --> 00:03:23.800
the most capable of ruling. She would be a
fair and loving ruler, and it's what she's

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:27.460
been striving for this whole series: to go
back home, to protect her home [...]"

00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:34.060
"I want you to help me, but I'll do it myself
if I have to."

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:38.280
Though she's frustrated by the way audiences
have reacted to the final season of Game of

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:42.440
Thrones, Turner isn't letting the negativity
stain her good memories of the series and

00:03:42.440 --> 00:03:45.550
what it was like to be a part of it. The actress
told The New York Times:

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:49.240
"One of the things that I'll remember the
most is just the camaraderie and the family

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:53.130
that we all created from being on the show.
I've never felt such a strong bond with a

00:03:53.130 --> 00:03:57.050
group of people in my life; I know that they're
going to be my family forever [...] I think

00:03:57.050 --> 00:03:58.320
that's what I'll take away the most."

